cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying dataset-generation pipeline, please cite both the software and the thesis."
title: "lbm-nca-thesis: Neural Cellular Automata for CFD in Architectural Design"
abstract: >-
  Research code for a neural-cellular-automata surrogate of steady-state
  mean wind flow around urban building layouts. The repository covers the
  full pipeline: procedural geometry generation with a 14-dimensional
  geometric descriptor (G_vec), a GPU lattice-Boltzmann (D2Q9 MRT-LES)
  solver that produces the ground-truth dataset, training of the neural
  cellular automaton surrogate, and a WebSocket bridge for real-time
  inference inside Rhino/Grasshopper.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ms-112-scott/lbm-nca-thesis"
keywords:
  - neural cellular automata
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - lattice Boltzmann method
  - surrogate model
  - urban wind environment
  - architectural design
  - Grasshopper
